[itemtooltip]
blueprintemptytip=Click [input=mouse2] to create a new blueprint
blueprintnonemptytip=Click [input=mouse1] to place this blueprint in the world\nClick [input=mouse2] to empty this blueprint (can't be restored)\nUse Pageup and Pagedown rotate the blueprint prior to placement\nBlueprint will not be consumed
blueprinttoolhelp=\n\n\nSelect the blueprint area by pressing [input=mouse1] and dragging.\n\nCtrl + [input=mouse1] a tile to exclude that tile type\nand the object at that cell, if any, from the blueprint.\n\nExcluded objects and tiles will not be part of the final blueprint\nand cannot be re-added after the blueprint is created.\n\nYou do not need to exclude every instance of the same object or tile.\nMarking one will exclude all instances of that same type.\n\nBlueprints can be renamed or edited in a Blueprint Workstation.\n\nEditing is limited to removing additional objects or tiles from the blueprint.\nTo change tiles or objects, or change blueprint dimensions, create a new blueprint instead.
projecterasertip=Click [input=mouse1] a placed blueprint project to cancel it.\nExisting construction will not be removed\nbut all jobs will be cancelled
inspectionglasstip=While selected in the hotbar, shows reinforcement levels when applicable.\n\nClick [input=mouse2] to <toggle> placed blueprint previews.
malignancegogglestip=While equipped, reveals tiles where hostile mobs can spawn
shallowholedig=\n\nClick [input=mouse2] on a raw dirt tile [item=dirttile] to dig a hole on the ground.\n
dirtpiletip=\n\nClick [input=mouse2] on a shallow hole [item=shallowholetile] to fill it with dirt, or\n[input=mouse2] on a charcoal pit to cover it with dirt.
treasureshovel=Can dig holes in caves.\n


